<title>RUSSIA: Russia to sell 11.5 trln rbls govt paper July 2.</title>
<headline>Russia to sell 11.5 trln rbls govt paper July 2.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will offer nine trillion roubles of GKO discount Treasury bills (series 21078) and 2.5 trillion roubles of an additional tranche of OFZ interest-bearing bonds with a fixed coupon (series 25001) on July 2, the central bank said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		    21078</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Issue date			 July 2, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor				364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    July 1, 1998</p>
<p>Full details of the bond auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		    25001</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     2.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date			 July 2, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)		704 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    June 6, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon date		June 6, 1998</p>
<p>    Coupon rate			20 pct</p>
<p>    Accruals			   14,247 rbls</p>
<p>On July 2, the Finance Ministry will also repay 8.29 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 203-day T-bills (series 22062).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
